cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OpenNeuroAtlas in your research, systematic review, or software workflow, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "OpenNeuroAtlas: A Living Open-Science Registry for Neurosurgery, Neuroimaging, Neuro-Oncology, and Surgical AI"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-19"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/openneuroatlas/openneuroatlas"
url: "https://openneuroatlas.github.io/openneuroatlas/"
abstract: >-
  OpenNeuroAtlas is a zero-build, PR-extensible GitHub Pages open-science
  registry and gap-analysis observatory cataloging open-access datasets,
  foundation models and clinical toolkits, and MICCAI / open benchmarks across
  neurosurgery, neuroimaging, neuro-oncology, and surgical AI. Governed by a
  single machine-readable JSON schema, it provides interactive Modality x
  Pathology coverage heatmaps, automated open-science gap detection,
  side-by-side cohort comparison, reproducible platform fetch snippets, and
  instant BibTeX, RIS, APA 7th, Markdown, and CSV export.
authors:
  - name: "OpenNeuroAtlas Contributors"
keywords:
  - open-science
  - neurosurgery
  - neuroimaging
  - neuro-oncology
  - surgical-ai
  - medical-imaging
  - datasets
  - foundation-models
  - miccai-benchmarks
  - metadata-registry
  - reproducible-research
